<title>USA: Apple plans to name Jobs chairman-report.</title>
<headline>Apple plans to name Jobs chairman-report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer Inc is planning to name company co-founder Steven Jobs as its next chairman, the San Francisco Chronicle reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to the story, Apple intends to announce Jobs as successor to former chairman and chief executive Gilbert Amelio at the Macworld Expo trade show in Boston next week.</p>
<p>Amelio was forced out of both posts earlier this month by Apple's board. Apple has hired an executive search firm to locate a chief executive.</p>
<p>The Chronicle story, which quotes Apple and Silicon Valley &quot;insiders,&quot; said Jobs' assignment is not assured, and that the company may opt for another candidate as chairman.</p>
<p>The Chronicle said Apple declined comment.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
